WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:07.414
The Simulation Arena holds ten scenarios. Each one has a stated objective, editable parameters and live metrics.

2
00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:15.419
Scenario C puts a brick partition in the room. Links that cross it lose most of the body shadowing contrast.

3
00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:29.357
Raising the partition loss to 30 dB removes information. The view warns that the empty room calibration is now stale.

4
00:00:30.254 --> 00:00:40.254
Scenario D uses concrete walls and a coherent back projection model. Strong reflections create ghost energy away from the person.

5
00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:50.541
Scenario E has three people crossing paths. Identity switches and fragmented tracks are counted, not hidden.

6
00:00:55.690 --> 00:01:04.690
The failure lab pushes the system out of its depth. With only two nodes there is one link, so the model refuses to localise.

7
00:01:08.062 --> 00:01:17.062
The learned ridge model was trained for one room layout. In a different room it reports unexpected geometry and does not run.

8
00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:29.427
The transformer slot has no trained weights, so selecting it produces an explained failure instead of output.

9
00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:41.163
Compare with baseline runs a second engine on the same seed. Both views share the timestamp.

10
00:01:56.971 --> 00:02:05.971
With half the packets gone, the current run degrades while the baseline keeps its accuracy. The table shows both.

11
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.665
The research workbench runs ablations. Every variant uses the same seed and the same input, unpaced in a worker.

12
00:02:10.665 --> 00:02:20.665
Here temporal smoothing is switched on and off. Accuracy and processing cost are reported side by side.

13
00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:43.049
Side by side reconstruction shows ground truth, a baseline model and the current model with one shared camera.

14
00:02:48.839 --> 00:02:57.839
Every model has a card: schemas, confidence semantics, limitations and evaluation on held out synthetic scenes.

15
00:02:57.939 --> 00:03:06.939
Hardware readiness is kept apart from the simulation. A checklist tests a real device before anything is claimed to work.

16
00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:13.940
Physical capture needs operator authorisation and consent, and raw recording is off unless someone turns it on.
